AUDIO: 'in this video and I\'ll show you how to edit any image using the Creal 2 model. I\'ll also teach you a new trick to fix blurry images using the Wen 2.1 VAE upscaler. So, first we need to install a custom node for Creal 2 edit. And let me tell'

[00:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'you, this is a third-party node and you can\'t find it in the ComfyUI library. Therefore, we must install it manually. And to do this, just follow my given'

[00:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'steps and copy the repository URL. Go to the custom nodes folder inside ComfyUI and open that folder in your command prompt. Type git clone and paste the URL and'

[00:37] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'just press enter. This will download the Creal 2 edit node and after that, you just restart your ComfyUI. That\'s it. Next, we need to download the LoRA file.'

[00:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'So, here, please download version 1.1. Do not download version 1. Why? Because it\'s the older version and you do not need it.'

[01:03] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'You will see two compressed versions of this file, rank 128 and rank 64. If you use the rank 128 version, you\'ll get about 94% of the quality of'

[01:15] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'uncompressed version. Keep in mind that a lower rank means lower quality. So, if your computer has low VRAM, you should use the rank 128 version.'

[01:27] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Otherwise, you can download the standard version 1.1. After you download the file, save it inside your ComfyUI\'s models LoRAs folder.'

[01:39] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Now, let\'s set up our models in ComfyUI. For this workflow, load the Creal 2 Turbo FP8 model. In the LoRA loader, select the Creal 2'

[01:51] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'identity edit LoRA. For the text encoder, you need Coin VL, and for the VAE, select the Coin image VAE. Once you install the custom node, you'

[02:03] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'will find two new nodes on your screen. The first is Create to Edit Model Patch, and the second one is Create to Edit Grounded Encode. The model patch node has options for'

[02:16] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'source latent and source latent B. The grounded encode node has options for image and image B. So, here, because we are editing only one image, connect your image to the'

[02:28] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'first image and source latent inputs. You do not need the B inputs unless you want to edit using two reference images. Next, connect these nodes to your'

[02:40] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'sampler, and now we are ready to test our workflow. Now, let\'s run our very first edit test. Load your starting image into the workflow.'

[02:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Here, I\'ll use a photo of a woman wearing gray shorts. So, before you type your prompt, I\'ll give you a helpful tip. Use clear action words like change, replace, add, or remove.'

[03:06] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Do not use vague words like transform. And for this test, let\'s use the prompt, "Change her gray shorts to bright red shorts." When you run this prompt, the model'

[03:19] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'successfully changes her shorts to red. However, the final image might look blurry. And if you get a blurry image, the problem is usually your image'

[03:31] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'resolution. If your image resolution is not divisible by eight, the output will look blurry. And to fix this, use the resize image and masking node to scale your image by'

[03:44] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'a multiple of eight. Even with the correct resolution, the edit might make your image look a bit dark or lose some sharpness. And to fix this, lower your lower'

[03:56] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'strength from one down to 0.75. This makes the image look sharper and keeps it closer to your original photo. Now, let\'s try a different edit.'

[04:08] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'We\'ll add a pair of black designer sunglasses to her face. When you edit a face, I suggest increasing your grounding resolution to 1280.'

[04:20] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'This higher setting helps the sunglasses blend into her face naturally. And if you want to give the AI more freedom to make changes, you can lower the grounding resolution to 512. If you do not want the original image to'

[04:35] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'change too much, keep this value higher. What I love about this model is it adds the sunglasses without changing the woman\'s face at all. Now, let\'s try a harder test.'

