[05:28] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'However, here I found a helpful rule. When you change large textured areas like carpets or floors, use a lower strength of one.'

[05:41] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'If you edit details on a face, keep the lower strength lower. Setting this LORA strength to one gives you a much better carpet texture. And to fix the missed area behind the'

[05:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'woman, we do not need to use a manual mask. Instead, we can solve this simply by updating our prompt. So, here what have I done is I updated our prompt to be more'

[06:06] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'specific. As you can see, the missing area is now completely fixed in our result. So, if the model misses a specific area, make sure to describe that area clearly'

[06:19] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'in your prompt. This simple trick works well without needing extra masks. So, sometimes what happens is two images have the exact same resolution, but one'

[06:32] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'still comes out blurry, while the other works very well. If you still get a blurry image, try manually changing the height of your image to 1280. And when I did this, the blur was mostly'

[06:46] [scene:talk]
